  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>Pattern 1</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Pattern. Step 0,1 dot. Step 1, 3 dots, 2 by 2 with upper left dot removed. Step 2, 5 dots, 3 by 2 with upper left dot removed. Step 3, 7 dots, 4 by 2 with upper left dot removed."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/d40bf31a833606cb35897e28384bce0fad6c41e6"/></media></figure></para>
<para>Pattern 2</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Pattern. Step 0, 0 dots. Step 1, 1 dot. Step 2, 4 dots, arranged 2 by 2. Step 3, 9 dots, arranged 3 by 3."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/32e3f0ae641cc7113cbd7ee68d29febdea28d604"/></media></figure></para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Look at Pattern 1.</para>
    <para> How is the number of dots in each step changing?</para>
      </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Each step has 2 rows of dots, with each row having the same number of dots as the step number, plus one extra
      dot.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> How many dots will be in Step 5 in the pattern, and how will they be arranged?</para>
      </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>In Step 5, there will be 2 rows of 5 dots plus one additional dot.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Look at Pattern 2.</para>
    <para> How is the number of dots in each step changing?</para>
      </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Each step has as many rows and columns of dots as the step number.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> How many dots will be in Step 5 in the pattern, and how will they be arranged?</para>
      </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Step 5 is a 5-by-5 array of dots.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

