<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Explain why the graphs of the two patterns look the way they do.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>The points representing the first pattern lie on a line because getting from one step to the next involves adding
      the same number of dots (2 dots). The points representing the second pattern do not lie on a line. They
      “curve” upward because the number of dots added at each step increases from step to step.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
